sts/unit + tests/interfaces' phrasing with the concrete oracle paths: tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py (cycle detection / _get_all_blocked_by) and tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py (detect_newly_unblocked), plus whatever suite covers _find_direct_blockers.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The pure `bfs(starts, neighbors_fn) -> set[str]` skeleton is under-specified for the two target functions, which return structurally different results: `_get_all_blocked_by` returns its `blocked` set (which is NOT the visited set — `_graph.py:151` adds every blocks-target to `blocked` before any existence check, so it can include nonexistent ids never dequeued, and the seed `ticket_id` is in `visited` but not in `blocked`), while `check_cycle_at_level` returns a bool via a mid-loop early return. A generic bfs returning the visited set cannot reproduce `blocked`; and if it returned `visited` (which contains the start node) it would change `check_would_create_cycle`'s membership test (`target_id in _get_all_blocked_by(source_id)`).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1daab2f01e65730","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (graph/_relations.py bfs helper) / _graph.py:127-182, 223-276","norm_id":"ndd65663373d6f416","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Define bfs so the returned set is an accumulator fed by neighbors_fn (each discovered neighbor id added regardless of whether it is later visited/exists), NOT the visited set — matching _get_all_blocked_by's `blocked`; for check_cycle_at_level compute the full reachable set and test `source_id in result` (order-independent, so the mid-loop early return is safely equivalent).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"cae8355903c4f9b8","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["2fb5c7fca361d01a",7958],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["c441159a7c1b10a2",6],"ticket_id":["b35de5